@startuml
title NestJS — fronteira HTTP interna e leitura por capability (NEST-HTTP 1.5.0)
actor "Cliente não autenticado" as Guest
actor "Backend interno confiável" as Service
actor "Cliente com capability" as User
participant "Nest Router HTTP" as Router
participant "InternalServiceGuard" as Internal
participant "RouteReadGuard" as Read
participant "HMAC route-access-policy" as Token
participant "Routes / Maps Services" as Backend
collections "MongoDB / Kafka / Google Maps" as External

Guest -> Router : POST /routes ou GET /places (sem bearer)
Router -> Internal : canActivate()
Internal --> Router : UnauthorizedException 401
Router --> Guest : 401 sem efeito externo

Service -> Router : POST /routes ou GET /directions
Bearer token interno
Router -> Internal : compara token com segredo configurado
alt segredo ausente ou token incorreto
  Internal --> Router : 401
else token interno correto
  Internal --> Router : true
  Router -> Backend : operação de serviço
  Backend -> External : persistência, broker ou provider
  External --> Backend : resposta
  Backend --> Router : resultado
end
Router --> Service : status HTTP

User -> Router : GET /routes/{id} com capability
Router -> Read : valida Authorization e params.id
Read -> Token : readRouteAccessToken() HMAC/TTL/aud/scope/route
alt inválido ou routeId diferente
  Token --> Read : null ou rota divergente
  Read --> Router : 401
else mesma rota, escopo read/simulate
  Token --> Read : claims válidos
  Read --> Router : true
  Router -> Backend : findOne(id)
  Backend --> Router : detalhes autorizados
end
Router --> User : resposta

note bottom
Bearer interno NÃO é identidade de usuário;
emissor de capability e ACL multi-tenant permanecem pendentes.
Kafka interno continua fora da autorização HTTP.
end note
@enduml
